{"arrivo":"pl","origine":"ine-pro","origine_nome":"Proto-Indo-European","n":8,"n_alternative":3,"parole":[{"parola":"-as","pos":"suffix","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"masculine noun suffix","termine_origine":"*-os","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*-os","categoria":"ereditato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Proto-Indo-European *-os."},{"parola":"jugo","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"synonym of jarzmo","termine_origine":"*yugóm","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*yugóm","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":["cucina","agricoltura"],"via":"","testo":"Ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *yugóm. Compare Old Polish igo."},{"parola":"rupić","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"synonym of kąsać (“to bite, to sting”)","termine_origine":"*Hrewp-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*Hrewp-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Derived from Proto-Indo-European *Hrewp- (“to break, to tear up”). Compare Latvian rūpēt, Lithuanian rūpėti and Russian ру́пить (rúpitʹ)."},{"parola":"rydz","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"saffron milk cap (Lactarius deliciosus)","termine_origine":"*h₁rewdʰ-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*h₁rewdʰ-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Polish rydz. By surface analysis, back-formation from rydzy. Cognate with Bulgarian рижика (rižika), Russian ры́жик (rýžik). Compare Spanish robellón (distantly cognate via Proto-Indo-European *h₁rewdʰ-)."},{"parola":"warchlę","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"wild boar piglet","termine_origine":"*wérsēn","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*wérsēn","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From German Ferkel + -ę. Per Brückner, a native word, derived from Proto-Indo-European *wérsēn (“virile man, male animal”). Akin to Latin verrēs (“boar”), Latvian vērsis (“ox”), Lithuanian ver̃šis (“calf, ox”), Old Prussian werstian (“calf”), Sanskrit वृषन् (vṛ́ṣan, “male, bull, stallion”)."},{"parola":"debiut","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"or from; either","significato":"debut","termine_origine":"*bʰewd-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*bʰewd-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":["sport"],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"fr","nome":"French","termine":"début","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"frm","nome":"Middle French","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"fro","nome":"Old French","termine":"but","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"fro","nome":"Old French","termine":"butte","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"frk","nome":"Frankish","termine":"*but","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"bútr","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*butą","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*bʰewd-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"Borrowed from French début, from Middle French, derivative of desbuter (“to move, begin”), from des- + but (“mark, goal”), from Old French but (“aim, goal, end, target”), either from Old French butte (“mound, knoll, target”), from Frankish *but (“stump, log”), or from Old Norse bútr (“log, stump, bu"},{"parola":"gem","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"alternatively","significato":"game (part of a set)","termine_origine":"*men-","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*men-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":["sport"],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"en","nome":"English","termine":"game","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"enm","nome":"Middle English","termine":"game","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ang","nome":"Old English","termine":"gamen","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*gaman","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*gamaną","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*men-","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"Borrowed from English game, from Middle English game, gamen, gammen, from Old English gamen (“sport, joy, mirth, pastime, game, amusement, pleasure”), from Proto-West Germanic *gaman, from Proto-Germanic *gamaną (“amusement, pleasure, game”), from *ga- (collective prefix) + *mann- (“man”); or altern"},{"parola":"zendra","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"alternatively","significato":"synonym of zgorzelina (“mill scale”)","termine_origine":"","catena":[{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":["scienza","arte"],"via":"","alternative":[{"codice":"de","nome":"German","termine":"Zunder","categoria":"prestito"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"testo":"Borrowed from German Zunder. Alternatively, a common Slavic word, cognate with Czech sádra, Old Church Slavonic сядра (sjadra) and Serbo-Croatian седра, ultimately from Proto-Indo-European *sendʰro-."}]}